The city administrator may grant minor variances with conditions. Either the owner and/or occupant of the physical site upon which the owner and/or occupant desires a mobile food service unit to operate, or which a mobile food service unit operator wishes to conduct business thereon, when accompanied by written authorization from the property owner and/or occupant, may request a variance from the terms of this article, where such variance will not be contrary to the public interest and where, owing to special conditions, strict enforcement of the provisions of this article will, in an individual case, result in unnecessary hardship; provided, however, that the spirit of this article shall be observed, and public safety and welfare secured. Such variance may be granted in an individual case upon a finding by the city administrator that:
